      "hints": [
        "General term: $\\binom{5}{r}\\left(\\frac{1}{ax}\\right)^{5-r}(2ax^2)^r = \\binom{5}{r} 2^r a^{2r-5} x^{3r-5}$.",
        "Set $3r - 5 = 1 \\implies r = 2$.",
        "Equate $\\binom{5}{2} 2^2 a^{-1} = \\frac{40}{a} = 5$ to find $a = 8$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term $T_{r+1}$ in the binomial expansion of $\\left(\\frac{1}{ax} + 2ax^2\\right)^5$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{5}{r}\\left(\\frac{1}{ax}\\right)^{5-r}(2ax^2)^r = \\binom{5}{r}\\left(\\frac{1}{a^{5-r}x^{5-r}}\\right)(2^r a^r x^{2r}) = \\binom{5}{r}2^r a^{2r-5}x^{3r-5}$$",
        "To find the term in $x = x^1$, equate the power of $x$ to $1$:\n$$3r - 5 = 1 \\implies 3r = 6 \\implies r = 2$$",
        "Evaluate the coefficient for $r = 2$ and equate to $5$:\n$$\\binom{5}{2}2^2 a^{4-5} = 10(4)a^{-1} = \\frac{40}{a} = 5$$\n$$5a = 40 \\implies a = 8$$"
      ],
